{"id": "docs/index.html:html-35", "file": "docs/index.html", "location": "html-35", "text": "Sleep", "sha256": "d466bcf52eb6921b1e747e51bf2cc1441926455ba146ecc477bed1574e44f9c0", "line": 123}
{"id": "docs/index.html:html-36", "file": "docs/index.html", "location": "html-36", "text": "The Heart screen, showing heart rate and HRV trends", "sha256": "6960f57dd5ecae37cc3f010cb70da9a0b60fdde1c39a660be3a184bb99198f26", "line": 126, "attribute": "alt"}
{"id": "docs/index.html:html-37", "file": "docs/index.html", "location": "html-37", "text": "Heart", "sha256": "770af9d180375fa9c3d29a50c124a04f538b277e1ed94ec20be8e244820d6534", "line": 127}
{"id": "docs/index.html:html-38", "file": "docs/index.html", "location": "html-38", "text": "The weekly Recap screen", "sha256": "de2ddbb21addcc5fe70570ae32ff4cc3835de5d38c246a3cef47d9ea4b4546d7", "line": 130, "attribute": "alt"}
{"id": "docs/index.html:html-39", "file": "docs/index.html", "location": "html-39", "text": "Recap", "sha256": "31056c37942fe3229f81be29d6f84a6b6d060789682d5be337b412f536630138", "line": 131}
{"id": "docs/index.html:html-40", "file": "docs/index.html", "location": "html-40", "text": "Every screenshot is real output from a WHOOP 4.0.", "sha256": "2343a1053236c030a8e8292183b9c956251e6fbd62750a2b371b008708065b6b", "line": 134}
{"id": "docs/index.html:html-41", "file": "docs/index.html", "location": "html-41", "text": "It runs on your phone", "sha256": "9116641b4a5b08f9a90dbe98a7c7b8a35ec786926a4fb6ef66ab970f18f4dde6", "line": 138}
{"id": "docs/index.html:html-42", "file": "docs/index.html", "location": "html-42", "text": "The band talks to the app, the app decodes the bytes and computes every metric\n          locally, and the results are stored on the device. There’s no server that\n          sees your health data — that isn’t a setting, it’s the\n          architecture.", "sha256": "6078d5e7a5bd131c433e374eee720d2fe9f012092c59219be662d7c5815e19be", "line": 139}
{"id": "docs/index.html:html-43", "file": "docs/index.html", "location": "html-43", "text": "Precisely, because “no cloud” gets said too loosely: GitHub Release\n          builds send anonymous crash diagnostics by default (switchable off); store\n          builds send none. Neither ever includes health data.", "sha256": "28dea27bb75f6b164fe4434eacff4859d177820219488894ce6b109dcd0c5ef5", "line": 145}
{"id": "docs/index.html:html-44", "file": "docs/index.html", "location": "html-44", "text": "Detail →", "sha256": "bb33666f61a49749ca3ca6187ef4f2ab76cbd9dfe43ff148f676b4d6d19f0fc5", "line": 149}
{"id": "docs/index.html:html-45", "file": "docs/index.html", "location": "html-45", "text": "Published methods, cited", "sha256": "cd10021eb697647be48ec665cff25768f53eb8bbe4e858c2916a9fb0ee480ffd", "line": 153}
{"id": "docs/index.html:html-46", "file": "docs/index.html", "location": "html-46", "text": "Banister TRIMP, Cole–Kripke, Lomb–Scargle, van Hees and friends.\n          Nothing invented, no neural net guessing at WHOOP’s formulas. You can go\n          read the paper and decide whether you trust the number.", "sha256": "d67c2142764f5bdab79601d877ffdf4625b238286aeda376a7e8d2d2c3337831", "line": 154}
{"id": "docs/index.html:html-47", "file": "docs/index.html", "location": "html-47", "text": "It admits what it doesn’t know", "sha256": "5f7cda2d1269f8ba7867a2f2a936ca6dd834a22343e14006e7f9de38e2749cd9", "line": 161}
{"id": "docs/index.html:html-48", "file": "docs/index.html", "location": "html-48", "text": "Every metric carries a confidence and a tier. When the data isn’t there\n          you get a dash, not a plausible-looking guess. SpO", "sha256": "0b240170d30978e43712cc7b51018f76255247f9a18ec654c58a3f2688c7b137", "line": 162}
{"id": "docs/index.html:html-49", "file": "docs/index.html", "location": "html-49", "text": "and skin\n          temperature are relative-only, because that’s what the band actually\n          gives up.", "sha256": "487d76009147de441a0a7b9a0edf1ae9e6df2306adbf20a9404d03a3a479c40d", "line": 164}
{"id": "docs/index.html:html-50", "file": "docs/index.html", "location": "html-50", "text": "Not a WHOOP clone", "sha256": "1708e57bad9185231b9f0059b11730bca2f0a30fef1740c3e2f1b39524092dec", "line": 170}
{"id": "docs/index.html:html-51", "file": "docs/index.html", "location": "html-51", "text": "Different algorithms, different numbers. They have years of research and a\n          team; this is textbook methods over a reverse-engineered byte stream. It trends\n          correctly and it’ll tell you when you’re under-recovered. It\n          isn’t their secret sauce and never claims to be.", "sha256": "f62f35e47c2324e0708f7837cd4430fa3d224e867c2ab423b0209754112c9124", "line": 171}
{"id": "docs/index.html:html-52", "file": "docs/index.html", "location": "html-52", "text": "Before you install", "sha256": "b39869a1169bf96e6657d69f134ce057fb49b1d0bac21847901abad58b8cd208", "line": 181}
{"id": "docs/index.html:html-53", "file": "docs/index.html", "location": "html-53", "text": "Quit the official WHOOP app before pairing.", "sha256": "c0f0211680a0d021f21f59c37f15c25e88effc3896f21e6d9f7664408ad914be", "line": 183}
{"id": "docs/index.html:html-54", "file": "docs/index.html", "location": "html-54", "text": "Bluetooth only lets one app own the band at a time.", "sha256": "9dc1e9420f622b8354afc80d615c309a628026c8c1f35a36071fc866c9762a42", "line": 183}
{"id": "docs/index.html:html-55", "file": "docs/index.html", "location": "html-55", "text": "Pick one and stay on it.", "sha256": "ba381c719acec8b33ee80ca2b062a9167ccdebda7833569d8b03e84e1f0883fc", "line": 184}
{"id": "docs/index.html:html-56", "file": "docs/index.html", "location": "html-56", "text": "A firmware push from the official app could change the records this depends on, and there’s no fixing that from here.", "sha256": "3668bec3c8bd8ec587058da52cbba97f8e7ce32cbffb40088bd4c53281fc0ea4", "line": 184}
{"id": "docs/index.html:html-57", "file": "docs/index.html", "location": "html-57", "text": "Not medical-grade.", "sha256": "cb404b86aa78bbe2b7b1b85c91586683155d79b43f40c86ae542fd78035d94e8", "line": 185}
{"id": "docs/index.html:html-58", "file": "docs/index.html", "location": "html-58", "text": "These are approximations from published research, not validated against a lab. Nothing here is a diagnosis.", "sha256": "ae500c83538480801d63928f2be85d925a5224eaa0267b83c92a26df309051d4", "line": 185}
{"id": "docs/index.html:html-59", "file": "docs/index.html", "location": "html-59", "text": "There are bugs.", "sha256": "9aecabb644c330f687065161b312745b6bb12dc00d7d8181496536b6563b8e70", "line": 186}
{"id": "docs/index.html:html-60", "file": "docs/index.html", "location": "html-60", "text": "It’s a beta built by one person.", "sha256": "c684cefb28d4049a774e785900bd405d16d2a8d234ee7ea4fd1082d0519642e4", "line": 186}
{"id": "docs/index.html:html-61", "file": "docs/index.html", "location": "html-61", "text": "Open an issue", "sha256": "c76d7d7c427b772356c9a9ac870f84f7887352b663c144ed0938816f1f556ab2", "line": 186}
{"id": "docs/index.html:html-62", "file": "docs/index.html", "location": "html-62", "text": "when something looks wrong — that’s genuinely the most useful thing you can do.", "sha256": "3a07a82ecb2759c1224a6b5acab49a4ff425b406cc9cf03e694109400e5362d4", "line": 186}
{"id": "docs/index.html:html-63", "file": "docs/index.html", "location": "html-63", "text": "How it’s put together", "sha256": "18311b88e7e06021504e9da0292cd0badc5b44a9231e0782be4311cddfc97275", "line": 191}
{"id": "docs/index.html:html-64", "file": "docs/index.html", "location": "html-64", "text": "band → Bluetooth → protocol decoder → local storage → analytics → the UI", "sha256": "ce51942e22d7b0096f08f48a6ea9f40efdfc8814893281ae8bf56d032ed3692a", "line": 192}
{"id": "docs/index.html:html-65", "file": "docs/index.html", "location": "html-65", "text": "edge", "sha256": "a1cb100f57e971cacf269e7c26e4630a25a8e9d4bdd35e32df1a80b66b896254", "line": 194}
{"id": "docs/index.html:html-66", "file": "docs/index.html", "location": "html-66", "text": "The app. Bluetooth, storage, the compute pipeline, every screen.", "sha256": "7e6aae3dc8a9d0ea10a5f12072519aa28781fbd93dd4cfd57272018d5bd8e7c1", "line": 196}
{"id": "docs/index.html:html-67", "file": "docs/index.html", "location": "html-67", "text": "protocol", "sha256": "2ea88c7a30351b12a4dcfc06cdce2af6eab18416176466c2500cb6ef74f745bf", "line": 198}
{"id": "docs/index.html:html-68", "file": "docs/index.html", "location": "html-68", "text": "The decoders. Raw band bytes into named fields. Pure Dart, zero dependencies.", "sha256": "92fece36f72c0e80e8bd47598297488155e3fc609ff50c24029cda93768d1960", "line": 200}
{"id": "docs/index.html:html-69", "file": "docs/index.html", "location": "html-69", "text": "analytics", "sha256": "65f98121a162a56ad8ee919ed9ea394b9eabd8714616acf30636c6092ee350b9", "line": 202}
{"id": "docs/index.html:html-70", "file": "docs/index.html", "location": "html-70", "text": "The math. Published, peer-reviewed methods with citations in the code.", "sha256": "bbf78eb01b8e84620d855d8050e0beece56df3c9dfbf4fa887af7d63d0248800", "line": 204}
{"id": "docs/index.html:html-71", "file": "docs/index.html", "location": "html-71", "text": "research", "sha256": "66f62d1807d3821a3865f2573b69c74be033f1341240ac861fefc6d430bff5e0", "line": 206}
{"id": "docs/index.html:html-72", "file": "docs/index.html", "location": "html-72", "text": "The lab notebook. The protocol written down, plus a Python client.", "sha256": "289078e5266f2569dfbeaa899ee1f3670e6fc75d46a7bec968f3b9f2c29fd233", "line": 208}
{"id": "docs/index.html:html-73", "file": "docs/index.html", "location": "html-73", "text": "Where it’s got to", "sha256": "7d887b2c8476577c9b654576a0ede0e183dc679cd452451cd94ef2980c78d6f6", "line": 214}
